WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.536
We are currently standing in front
of a fence, which is known as the Fence.

2
00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.139
This is one of the oldest
campus traditions that we have,

3
00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.608
and the story is that
where we are currently standing

4
00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:11.277
was a common meeting
ground for students from 

5
00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:13.246
the Margaret Morison Carnegie
College for Women

6
00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:16.282
and men from the then
Carnegie Technical Schools.

7
00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:19.619
The school decided to put up a fence
one day for students to socialize,

8
00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:24.190
and one random night a fraternity decided
to paint the fence to advertise a party.

9
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.793
And then the fence painting tradition
kind of stuck.

10
00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:29.796
Today, this fence holds the record
as one of the most painted

11
00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:33.833
objects of all time, and we use it
as a rotating billboard to paint messages,

12
00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:38.833
everything from happy birthday to marriage
proposals to club advertisements.

13
00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.673
A few notes on fence rules.

14
00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:45.078
Only those affiliated with the University
can paint it, and painting only happens

15
00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:48.314
under the shroud of darkness,
which is defined as from midnight to sunrise.

16
00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:52.185
And it must be done by hand
with no spray paint or other technologies.

17
00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:55.622
Otherwise it will be considered
as vandalism and a fine will be incurred.

18
00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:59.259
Students will guard the fence the night
before to reserve the right to paint it.

19
00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:02.228
Another tradition that we have on
campus is called Carnival,

20
00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:05.498
where this entire grassy area
gets filled with carnival rides

21
00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.802
and food from Thursday
through Sunday in the spring semester.

22
00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.603
During this time, students will build

23
00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:14.641
elaborate one or two story buildings
and they are called booths.

24
00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.976
Also, during Carnival we have buggy races.

25
00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:20.313
This is basically a five legged-relay,
except instead of batons,

26
00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:23.483
there is this torpedo-shaped cart
with the student inside

27
00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:27.620
and these can reach
maximum speeds of up to 35 miles per hour.

